  "description": "Checks that every Python code block in a Markdown file actually compiles and runs, by extracting each block to a temporary file, executing it in an isolated subprocess, and writing a pass/fail report with per-snippet coverage. Use when the user asks to verify, test, or validate the code samples in a README, a guide, or a documentation page; wants to know which snippets in a Markdown file are broken or out of date; or asks for a snippet verification report. Don't use for running the project's test suite (run pytest directly), for checking code style or formatting (use `adk-style`), or for authoring a new runnable sample agent (use `adk-sample-creator`).",
